  "question": {
    "text": "For a certain reaction the variation of rate constant with temperature is given by the equation<br />\r<br />\r<math><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;where k<sub>0</sub>=k at zero degree centigrade<br />\r<br />\rThe value of temperature coefficient of the reaction is -"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0.1</mn></math>",
